  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering the Ethiopian Human Rights Commission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support is to target identified challenges that fall into three clusters: organisational arrangements concerning formal mandate of the Ethiopian Human Rights Commission and its founding legislation, adequate budget provided by the Ethiopian Parliament and overall reform, restructuring, ICT infrastructures, and strategic planning of the Commission. The second dimension ( human rights competences) addresses capacities at the organisational level, physical and technological infrastructures, strategic leadership and expertise. The third dimension concerns the catalyst function, which includes the Commission&#x2019;s engagement with national, regional and international human rights bodies and actors. To effectively tackle the human rights concerns and strengthen the human rights landscape in Ethiopia, it is important to strengthen the Commission. This highlights the justification for, and importance of, the partnership with DIHR, which aims to capacitate the Commission to become an independent NHRI.</narrative>
  </description>
